Fixed the wraparound in `include/ringbuf/ring_buffer.hpp`. When the buffer was full, `push` overwrote the oldest slot but never advanced `tail_`, so after the first wrap `pop()` returned the newest element first and `size()` kept growing past `capacity()`.

```cpp
void push(T value) {
    buffer_[head_] = std::move(value);
    head_ = (head_ + 1) % capacity_;
    if (size_ == capacity_) {
        tail_ = (tail_ + 1) % capacity_;  // drop the oldest
    } else {
        ++size_;
    }
}
```

